<article class="env-remark" id="0CXH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CXH">Remark <span data-tag="0CXH">98.9.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $p : \mathcal{X} \to (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ be a category fibred in groupoids. Let $\xi = (R, \xi _ n, f_ n)$ be a formal object. Set $k = R/\mathfrak m$ and $x_0 = \xi _1$. The formal object $\xi $ defines a formal object $\xi $ of the predeformation category $\mathcal{F}_{\mathcal{X}, k, x_0}$. This follows immediately from Definition <a href="/tag/07X4" data-tag="07X4">98.9.1</a> above, Formal Deformation Theory, Definition <a href="/tag/06H3" data-tag="06H3">90.7.1</a>, and our construction of the predeformation category $\mathcal{F}_{\mathcal{X}, k, x_0}$ in Section <a href="/tag/07T2" data-tag="07T2">98.3</a>. </p>
</article>